          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شوخ (shukh) — \"witty, playful\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "آموزگار ما خیلی شوخ است و کلاس را شاد میکند. âmuzgâr-e mâ kheyli shukh ast va kelâs râ shâd mikonad. Our teacher is very witty and cheers up the class."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "shukhi 'a joke' and shukhi kardan 'to joke' are built on it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "shukh is usually taken as a native Persian word, and shukhi, 'a joke', is built on it. No source used here gives its older form, and its origin is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
